# Future-Lock Wasp

Not a combat encounter. An environmental hazard.

Small. Amber-gold with dark banding. The abdomen tapers to an unusual point — not a stinger in the conventional sense, but a specialized appendage that injects metamorphosis venom. Found in the Turnroot Weald, nesting in root cavities and beneath the bark of older trees.

Individually: harmless. As a swarm: a Future-Lock event.

---

## Future-Lock Venom

The venom interrupts what a body was about to do next. In combat terms it is the keyword **Future-Lock** (`rules/card-glossary.md`): the stung creature's hand size drops, and stays dropped for the rest of the fight.

Outside a fight the same venom makes the hands slow and the next action arrive a half-beat late — enough that a navigation check or a careful harvest can fail for no obvious reason. The mechanical weight is in combat; the fiction is continuous.

---

## Swarm Trigger

Wasps do not attack unless a nest is disturbed. Nests are found in root cavities, beneath bark overhang, and occasionally anchored to the underside of fallen logs. They do not announce themselves.

On disturbance, a swarm lifts. Each character in the area makes a **2d10 + Body save**.

| Result | Consequence |
|--------|-------------|
| 15+ | No sting — evaded cleanly |
| 10–14 | Future-Lock 1 (hand size −1 for the rest of the next combat, or this one if already in a fight) |
| 5–9 | Future-Lock 2 |
| Below 5 | Future-Lock 3 |

The swarm persists for up to 3 rounds in the disturbed area. Each round spent in the area requires a new save; applications stack. Moving out of the nest zone ends further checks.

If the party is not in combat when stung, track the stacks and apply them at the start of the next combat (hand size reduced before the first draw of that fight). A long rest clears unspent stacks that never reached a fight.

---

## Dispersal

The swarm has counters. Characters who find them don't get stung again.

**Fire:** Any open flame presented toward the swarm disperses it immediately. No further saves required. Fire does not need to hit the wasps — the light and heat drives them off.

**Full submersion in water:** Wasps will not follow into water. Submerged characters take no further saves. The swarm hovers at the surface for 1 round then disperses if no other targets are present.

**Leaving the area:** Move out of the nest zone. One final save on the round of departure, then the swarm returns to the nest.

---

## Named Nest Site — The Hanging Gallery

Deep in the Weald, a cluster of old trees with heavily grooved bark hosts a permanent colony. The bark overhangs create natural alcoves — each one contains a nest. The canopy here is dense enough that fire is risky (DM discretion on whether torch use threatens to spread).

This is a named hazard site, not a combat encounter. Parties scouting the gallery carefully (DC 13 Mind/Reason) can identify the nests before disturbing them. Parties moving quickly or distracted by the forest customs will not.

---

## Harvest — Larvae

DC 14 Body/Senses to extract larvae without triggering the swarm. A dispersed swarm leaves nests unguarded for 1 minute — free harvest window.

**Loot:** Future-Lock Wasp Larvae. See `items/turnroot-weald-items.md`. Senshi's rate assumes live delivery within a day.

